<title>FRANCE: Havas says no talks with U.S. ally.</title>
<headline>Havas says no talks with U.S. ally.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Havas chairman Pierre Dauzier said on Friday that no negotiations had started with a U.S. company about taking a stake in the French media group but he said there had been some initial &quot;contacts&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;There are contacts but no negotiation whatsoever has been started,&quot; Dauzier said in the margin of a shareholders' meeting of Canal Plus, in which Havas is a main shareholder.</p>
<p>Stock market rumours recently suggested a U.S. company - some reports suggested Time Warner Inc - could become a Havas shareholder.</p>
<p>Brokers say that Caisse des Depots et Consignations, with less than three percent, Paribas with 4.1 percent and Audiofina with 4.3 percent could be willing to sell their Havas stakes.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
